{'name': 'University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$18,530', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': "Published in-state tuition-and-fees estimate; the lower end of the university's $18,530-$24,018 in-state range, used as the general/base arts-and-sciences equivalent. The 2026-27 base schedule separately reports $13,252 resident tuition.", 'source_url': 'https://www.admissions.illinois.edu/tuition/'}
{'name': 'Indiana University Bloomington', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$12,143.88', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Full-time resident annual general undergraduate rate: $10,621.84 tuition plus $1,522.04 combined mandatory fee; excludes program differentials.', 'source_url': 'https://finance.iu.edu/doc/2025-2027-tuition-and-fee-schedule-recommended.pdf'}
{'name': 'University of Iowa', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$11,971.00', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Resident Liberal Arts & Sciences 12+-hour rate is $5,985.50 per semester (tuition plus listed mandatory fees), or $11,971 for fall and spring.', 'source_url': 'https://tuition.ais.its.uiowa.edu/'}
{'name': 'University of Maryland, College Park', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$12,835.00', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Full-time resident general undergraduate annual amount: $11,015 tuition plus $1,820 mandatory fees. Excludes junior/senior Business, Engineering, and Computer Science differential.', 'source_url': 'https://academiccatalog.umd.edu/undergraduate/fees-expenses-financial-aid/tuition-fees/'}
{'name': 'University of Michigan, Ann Arbor', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$18,896', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Michigan-resident lower-division (0-54 credits), LSA-based tuition-and-fees estimate for a first-year student; the university labels the figure Tuition & Fees.', 'source_url': 'https://admissions.umich.edu/costs-aid/costs'}
{'name': 'Michigan State University', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$18,071.00', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'General/core-unit freshman resident estimate: $8,828 tuition per semester plus $170 Recreational & Wellness Center charge and $37.50 student-voted taxes per semester. Excludes program-specific and section fees; core units include arts and letters, natural science, and social science.', 'source_url': 'https://controller.msu.edu/student-accounts/tuition-rates-by-semester/resident-undergrad-fall-spring'}
{'name': 'University of Minnesota Twin Cities', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$19,312', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Published undergraduate resident tuition-and-fees estimate for one academic year at the general resident rate; excludes Carlson/CSE-type surcharges.', 'source_url': 'https://onestop.umn.edu/finances/costs/cost-attendance'}
{'name': 'University of Nebraska–Lincoln', 'year': '2025-26 (latest located)', 'amount': '$11,100', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': '2026-27 was not located. Official undergraduate resident cost-of-attendance table labels this combined line Tuition & Fees; it is the published full-year general estimate rather than tuition alone, with rates otherwise varying by credits/program.', 'source_url': 'https://financialaid.unl.edu/cost/estimated-cost-attendance/2025-2026/'}
{'name': 'Northwestern University', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$73,062', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Private university; in-state status is not applicable. Calculated from full-time undergraduate tuition of $23,934 per quarter × 3, plus mandatory Associated Student Government fee ($98 × 3), Athletics Event Fee ($72/year), and Student Health Fee ($298 × 3). Excludes optional/defaultable NU-SHIP insurance and incidental charges.', 'source_url': 'https://www.northwestern.edu/sfs/tuition/undergraduate/'}
{'name': 'The Ohio State University (Columbus)', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$14,050', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'First-year Ohio-resident Columbus estimate; the official table says Tuition includes instructional and general fees. Regional-campus figures and program differentials are excluded.', 'source_url': 'https://undergrad.osu.edu/cost-and-aid/basic-costs'}
{'name': 'University of Oregon (Eugene)', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$18,044.74', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Incoming resident 2026 cohort at 45 credits/year: resident tuition $14,531.85 plus Eugene mandatory fees ($981 per term × 3) plus one-time new-student matriculation fee $569.89. Excludes program differentials and course-specific fees.', 'source_url': 'https://vpfa.uoregon.edu/tuition/undergraduate-2026-tuition-cohort-tuition-and-fees'}
{'name': 'Pennsylvania State University (University Park)', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$21,518', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Pennsylvania-resident freshman/sophomore full-time annual tuition is $20,878; mandatory Student Initiated Fee is $320 per semester for 9+ credits ($640 annually). Combined amount is $21,518. General lower-division rate; program-specific charges may apply.', 'source_url': 'https://tuition.psu.edu/tuition-schedules'}
{'name': 'Purdue University (West Lafayette)', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$9,992 per academic year', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Indiana-resident, full-time flat rate (8+ credits): General Service $9,718 plus Student Fitness and Wellness Fee $234 and Student Activity Fee $40. Program-specific fees can apply.', 'source_url': 'https://www.purdue.edu/treasurer/finance/bursar-office/tuition/fee-rates-2026-2027/undergraduate-tuition-and-fees-2026-2027/'}
{'name': 'Rutgers University–New Brunswick', 'year': 'Latest published (2025-26)', 'amount': '$19,389 per academic year', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': '2026-27 was not located in the consolidated public table. New Jersey-resident School of Arts and Sciences benchmark: tuition $15,381 plus fees $4,008; amounts vary by school/college.', 'source_url': 'https://admissions.rutgers.edu/costs-and-aid/tuition-fees'}
{'name': 'University of California, Los Angeles', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$16,430 per academic year', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'California-resident new undergraduate estimate: UC systemwide tuition $15,588 plus campus fees $842. Health insurance is separate. (California residency is the relevant in-state category.)', 'source_url': 'https://financialaid.ucla.edu/go/coa'}
{'name': 'University of Southern California', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$77,336 per academic year', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Private university; in-state status is not applicable. General undergraduate tuition is $75,384 for 12–18 units over two semesters plus $1,952 in fees; major-specific lab/studio charges may be additional.', 'source_url': 'https://financialaid.usc.edu/undergraduate-financial-aid/cost-of-attendance/'}
{'name': 'University of Washington (Seattle)', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$14,340 per academic year', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Washington-resident first-year Seattle undergraduate: resident tuition $12,664 plus annual student fees $1,676. Course fees and student insurance, where applicable, are additional.', 'source_url': 'https://www.washington.edu/opb/tuition-fees/estimated-annual-cost-of-attendance-for-first-year-undergraduates/'}
{'name': 'University of Wisconsin–Madison', 'year': '2026-27', 'amount': '$12,532 per academic year', 'includes_fees': 'Yes', 'notes': 'Wisconsin-resident estimated full-time, nine-month undergraduate tuition and fees; general rate excluding listed program tuition differentials. Loan fees are separate and excluded.', 'source_url': 'https://financialaid.wisc.edu/cost-of-attendance/'}

